The Codex adapter's tests check its messages against
crates/agents/schema/codex-app-server-0.166.0.contract.json, a cut of the JSON schema of the
app-server protocol of OpenAI Codex 0.166.0 (github.com/openai/codex, tag rust-v0.166.0). That
schema is part of OpenAI Codex, Copyright 2025 OpenAI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSE-APACHE); the file's "$comment" says what was changed. The upstream file it was cut from,
codex-rs/app-server-protocol/schema/json/codex_app_server_protocol.schemas.json at that tag, has the
SHA-256 9b6d53647b00d68a04181b826599025a810cfa78acb3ec4d518c68b4120499c0. The five sentences in
crates/agents/src/codex/rpc.rs (EXPIRED_SIGN_IN_MESSAGES) are quoted word for word from
codex-rs/login/src/auth/manager.rs at the same tag, under the same licence, so Archforge can
recognise them.
